  m_Name: Note_Audio_MaritimeIncidents1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  title: Environmental Oddities
  key: 12
  topic: 3
  boardContentText: Fog and tides behaved unpredictably
  boardSprite: {fileID: 0}
  contentText: "EMIL: My audio diary. Next entry.\n[pause]\nEMIL: The water keeps
    changing. Up, down. No pattern.\n[brief silence]\nEMIL: I can't get into the
    machinery room again. The tunnel is underwater. I've gone back three times. Three
    times the same.\n[pause]\nEMIL: And then there's the fog. Sometimes so thick
    I can't see one step ahead. Comes out of a clear sky. I'm standing at my front
    door \u2014 and before I step out, it's all around me.\n[longer silence]\nEMIL:
    Everything here behaves so strangely. Just... off.\n[pause]\nEMIL: ...Could this
    have something to do with the lighthouse? I've been playing with it. Changing
    the rotation speed. ...And then this.\n[brief silence]\nEMIL: But why would it
    have any effect? What does the spin of the beam have to do with water? With fog?\n[hesitation]\nEMIL:
    I don't understand it. ...I don't understand any of it.\n[click]"
  paperSprite: {fileID: 0}
